      "writtenOn": "2022-06-07T23:03:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve verified with this change and confirmed the WbsCallback gotten triggered before the SLC connected.\n```\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.265624Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: [7C:96:D2:8B:F8:BC]: hfp connected.\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.322245Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: gd/rust/topshim/hfp/hfp_shim.cc:105 - WbsCallback: WbsCallback 2 from 7c:96:d2:8b:f8:bc\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.363805Z WARNING btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: gd/rust/topshim/hfp/hfp_shim.cc:116 - AtCindCallback: Respond +CIND: 0,0,1,5,0,5,0 to AT+CIND? from 7c:96:d2:8b:f8:bc\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.442436Z INFO vm_concierge[6003]: BalloonTrace: { \"vm\": \"arcvm\", \"game_mode\": false, \"balloon\": 4435320832, \"guest_cached\": 1327165440, \"guest_unreclaimable\": 109436928, \"guest_free\": 320454656, \"target_free\": 320622592, \"host_available\": 3706049536, \"host_free\": 451104768, \"deflation_limit_1\": [0, 1049181184], \"deflation_limit_2\": [899, 1369259008], \"deflation_limit_3\": [999, 4015340544], \"delta\": -167936 }\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.450768Z WARNING btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: gd/rust/topshim/hfp/hfp_shim.cc:159 - AtBindCallback: AT+BIND 1,2 from addr 7c:96:d2:8b:f8:bc: Bluetooth HF Indicators is not supported.\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.493868Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: gd/rust/topshim/hfp/hfp_shim.cc:60 - ConnectionStateCallback: ConnectionStateCallback from 7c:96:d2:8b:f8:bc\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.493971Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: bt_btif_queue: btif/src/btif_profile_queue.cc:121 - queue_int_advance: queue_int_advance: removing connection request: address\u003dxx:xx:xx:xx:f8:bc UUID\u003d111F busy\u003dtrue\n2022-06-07T22:41:17.494048Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: [7C:96:D2:8B:F8:BC]: hfp slc connected.\n```\n\nThe first WbsCallback was triggered by the \"AT+BAC\" in the SLC setup process.\n\nThe codes are at https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;drc\u003dbbe77d66e7bee8bd1f0bc7e5492b5376b0207ef6;l\u003d562\n\n```\n    case BTA_AG_AT_BAC_EVT:\n      BTIF_TRACE_DEBUG(\"AG Bitmap of peer-codecs %d\", p_data-\u003eval.num);\n      /* If the peer supports mSBC and the BTIF preferred codec is also mSBC,\n      then\n      we should set the BTA AG Codec to mSBC. This would trigger a +BCS to mSBC\n      at the time\n      of SCO connection establishment */\n      if (p_data-\u003eval.num \u0026 BTM_SCO_CODEC_MSBC) {\n        BTIF_TRACE_EVENT(\"%s: btif_hf override-Preferred Codec to MSBC\",\n                         __func__);\n        BTA_AgSetCodec(btif_hf_cb[idx].handle, BTM_SCO_CODEC_MSBC);\n      } else {\n        BTIF_TRACE_EVENT(\"%s btif_hf override-Preferred Codec to CVSD\",\n                         __func__);\n        BTA_AgSetCodec(btif_hf_cb[idx].handle, BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD);\n      }\n```\n\n\nAnd, the callback got called again when the actual +BCS was triggered by the AG when setting up the data pipeline.\n\n```\n2022-06-07T22:41:31.290694Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: stack/btm/btm_sco.cc:454 - btm_send_connect_request: Sending eSCO connect request over handle:0x0100\n2022-06-07T22:41:31.290790Z WARNING btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: bta/ag/bta_ag_sco.cc:1098 - bta_ag_sco_event: SCO_state_change: [BTA_AG_SCO_CODEC_ST(0x02)]-\u003e[BTA_AG_SCO_OPENING_ST(0x03)] after event [BTA_AG_SCO_CN_DONE_E(0x03)]\n2022-06-07T22:41:31.290903Z INFO btadapterd[12026]: bluetooth: gd/rust/topshim/hfp/hfp_shim.cc:105 - WbsCallback: WbsCallback 2 from 7c:96:d2:8b:f8:bc\n```\n\nCodes:\n```\n    case BTA_AG_AT_BCS_EVT:\n      BTIF_TRACE_DEBUG(\"%s: AG final selected codec is 0x%02x 1\u003dCVSD 2\u003dMSBC\",\n                       __func__, p_data-\u003eval.num);\n      /* No BTHF_WBS_NONE case, because HF1.6 supported device can send BCS */\n      /* Only CVSD is considered narrow band speech */\n      bt_hf_callbacks-\u003eWbsCallback(\n          (p_data-\u003eval.num \u003d\u003d BTM_SCO_CODEC_CVSD) ? BTHF_WBS_NO : BTHF_WBS_YES,\n          \u0026btif_hf_cb[idx].connected_bda);\n      break;\n```\n\nSo, I think hfp_shim should have valid `wbs_supported` valueat SlcConnected. But, I do agree that we can add logics to handle the case that `+BCS: 2` failed and the stack falls back to CVSD, which is a known corner case instead of a synchronize work required for this change.",
